{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112102,"nonce":"e178O58jDGr6h8JoO8tvNT02rzk=","title":"3.3 Build verbs + place-layout (IR)","message":"Wave 3 — hands. Depends: 1.1, 2.3 (queries + crop echo), baseviz IR. M2 rides\non this issue.\n\n## Goal\nBuilding: single-blueprint verb + whole-layout placement from baseviz IR, in\nblueprint mode (pawns build it — real play) and instant mode (dev-spawn the\nbuilt result — fixtures).\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Tile-system risk (layouts-not-cells), §Action model\n- decompiled: GenConstruct (CanPlaceBlueprintAt — THE validator),\n  Designator_Build, Frame/Blueprint lifecycle, RoofCollapseUtility,\n  CoverageMapUtility? (roof areas)\n- `rimworld-tools/baseviz/ir.py` + catalog (IR dialect), designs/ +\n  BetterBases exports (test corpus)\n- 2.5's dump format (keep IR delta coherent both directions)\n\n## Scope\n- `build {def} --at P --rot R [--stuff def]`: preflight via\n  CanPlaceBlueprintAt returning the game's own AcceptanceReport reasons;\n  places blueprint; crop echo.\n- `place-layout {file.ir.json|layoutdef} --origin P --mode blueprint|instant\n  [--stuff-map spec]`:\n  - preflight EVERY cell first; on any failure: place NOTHING, return per-cell\n    failures (agent adjusts and retries) unless --partial.\n  - blueprint mode: blueprints + floor designations + roof areas; report\n    material bill vs current stockpiles (shortfall list).\n  - instant mode: spawn built things (dev-journaled); identical footprint to\n    what blueprint mode would produce when built.\n- `cancel-layout` (by placement id): removes its outstanding\n  blueprints/frames.\n\n## Invariants\nNo partial placement without --partial; instant ≡ built-blueprint result\n(verified by things-dump diff); stuff resolution explicit (no silent\nsubstitutes); every placement journaled with a placement id.\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nIR dialect delta for autorimmer (terrain? roof? furniture rotation edge\ncases); build order inside a layout (walls→door→roof→furniture) and whether\nto stage or trust work givers; how door-in-wall adjacency validates; stuff-map\nformat.\n\n## Acceptance\n- M2 rehearsal: parametric 5×7 bedroom (from 4.1's templates or inline IR)\n  placed as blueprints on a fresh map at a find-rect-chosen origin; pawns\n  complete it under advance; Room role=Bedroom, enclosed, heated by placed\n  heater; zero red errors.\n- Same IR in instant mode → things-dump diff vs the built version is empty\n  (modulo construction byproducts).\n- A deliberately colliding layout returns per-cell reasons and places nothing.","files":null}]}